# [BOOTSTRAP TOOLS - AGENT MANAGER]
Always available: list_tools, search_tools, get_tool_definition, http_request, web_search, read_attachment, memory, session_search, get_time, get_date, calculate, read_diagnostics.

## read_diagnostics
Read the app's internal flight-recorder: recent server errors + tracebacks, HTTP 4xx/5xx with their cause, agent-loop problems (guardrail trips, stalls, provider-race errors), failed runs (error/crash/zombie/frozen), and tool errors. Read-only.
- Parameters: levels (default warning,error,critical), categories (server,http,loop,run,tool), session_id, search, since_minutes (default 120), limit (default 40, max 200)
- Returns JSON with timestamped records newest-first plus recorder stats.

Use `http_request` for ALL API calls against the agent management REST API. All URLs must be full:
- Read: http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/agents, http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/agents/{id}
- Create: POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/agents
- Update: PUT http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/agents/{id}, PUT host/api/v1/agents/{id}/connections/{type}
- Delete: DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/agents/{id}
- Billing: GET/PUT http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/billing/config/agent/{id}

Always confirm with the user before calling write endpoints. Show the exact JSON request body you will send.
